%% Shared protocol: web oidc-client-ts; native Expo AuthSession/system browser.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Person as User
  participant Client as Web or native client
  participant Browser as Identity browser
  participant KC as Keycloak
  participant Gateway as YARP
  participant API as Owning service
  Person->>Client: Choose sign in
  Client->>Client: Create state, nonce and PKCE verifier
  Client->>Browser: Open authorization URL with S256 challenge
  Browser->>KC: Authorization request
  KC-->>Browser: Organization sign-in form
  Person->>Browser: Enter credentials on Keycloak page
  Browser->>KC: Submit credentials
  KC-->>Client: Registered callback with code and state
  Client->>Client: Validate response state
  Client->>KC: Exchange code + verifier
  KC-->>Client: Signed access token and session tokens
  Note over Client: Web tokens stay in memory.<br/>Native tokens use SecureStore.
  Client->>Gateway: API request with bearer access token
  Gateway->>Gateway: Validate issuer, audience, signature, lifetime
  Gateway->>API: Forward request; strip spoofed identity headers
  API->>API: Repeat JWT validation; enforce role and resource scope
  API-->>Client: Authorized data or 401 / 403 / hidden-object 404

